---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service - Ascend" description="Terms of Service for Ascend, the iOS stair-stepper workout tracker.">

  <style>
    .terms-page {
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top left, #2a2f3c 0, var(--bg) 55%);
    }

    .terms-page main {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 120px 24px 64px;
    }

    .terms-page h1 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-size: 36px;
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .last-updated {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 14px;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .terms-page h2 {
      font-size: 20px;
      margin: 36px 0 12px;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .terms-page p,
    .terms-page li {
      line-height: 1.7;
      font-size: 15px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .terms-page ul {
      padding-left: 20px;
      margin: 8px 0;
    }

    .terms-page li {
      margin: 6px 0;
    }

    .terms-page strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .terms-page a {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .terms-page a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .divider {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      margin: 40px 0;
    }

    .terms-footer-note {
      font-size: 13px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .terms-page main {
        padding: 100px 16px 48px;
      }

      .terms-page h1 {
        font-size: 28px;
      }

      .terms-page h2 {
        font-size: 18px;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="terms-page">
    <main>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="last-updated">Last updated: May 19, 2026</p>

      <h2>Agreement to Terms</h2>
      <p>By using Ascend, you agree to these Terms of Service and our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the app.</p>

      <h2>Use of Ascend</h2>
      <p>Ascend is a stairstepper workout tracking app. You are responsible for the information you enter, the workouts you log, and how you use the app during exercise.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use Ascend only for lawful personal fitness tracking purposes.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt to interfere with the app, backend services, leaderboards, or other users' accounts.</li>
        <li>Do not upload unlawful, harmful, or infringing photos, videos, notes, or profile content.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Health and Safety</h2>
      <p>Ascend provides fitness tracking and progress tools, not medical advice. Consult a qualified medical professional before starting or changing an exercise program, especially if you have a medical condition, injury, or health concern. Stop exercising and seek medical help if you feel pain, dizziness, shortness of breath, or other concerning symptoms.</p>

      <h2>Accounts and Authentication</h2>
      <p>You may sign in with supported authentication providers, including Apple and Google. You are responsible for keeping your account secure and for activity that occurs through your account.</p>

      <h2>Subscriptions and Paid Features</h2>
      <p>Ascend may offer subscriptions or paid features. Any purchase terms shown in the App Store at the time of purchase control billing, renewal, cancellation, and refunds.</p>

      <h2>User Content</h2>
      <p>You keep ownership of the workout notes, photos, videos, and other content you add to Ascend. You grant Ascend permission to store, process, display, back up, and sync that content as needed to provide the app.</p>

      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Ascend may integrate with services such as Apple HealthKit, Hevy, Firebase, and other providers. Your use of those services may also be governed by their own terms and privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>Service Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update, suspend, or discontinue parts of Ascend over time. We may also update these Terms by posting a revised version on this page and changing the last updated date.</p>

      <h2>Disclaimers and Limits</h2>
      <p>Ascend is provided as is and as available. To the fullest extent permitted by law, Ascend is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of the app.</p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about these Terms, please contact us at <a href="mailto:pavayt@gmail.com">pavayt@gmail.com</a>.</p>

      <hr class="divider" />
      <p class="terms-footer-note">Built by Tyler Pavay &middot; <a href="https://ascendstepper.com">ascendstepper.com</a></p>
    </main>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
